{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqeh1zs40t4","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Gate node type: dispatcher-created coordination primitive for operational dependencies","summary":"Design decision: introduce a \"gate\" node subtype for operational side-effects that block downstream work but are satisfied by external events (daemon restart, commit landing, human approval) rather than by a worker.\n\nKey properties:\n- gate_kind: \"daemon-restart\" | \"main-commit\" | \"human-approval\" | \"test-pass\" (extensible registry)\n- created_by: dispatcher (not worker — wiring is always the dispatcher's responsibility, Option B)\n- status lifecycle: not_ready → done, completed by a satisfier, not by a worker claiming the task\n- Each task that needs the gate creates its OWN gate instance (no shared hub node)\n- Dependents block on their own gate; one real-world event clears ALL standing gates of that kind\n\nDaemon-restart gate specifics:\n- On daemon startup: sweep all gates where kind=daemon-restart AND created_at < started_at, mark done\n- Timing guard: gates created AFTER current process started must wait for NEXT restart\n- Completion summary: \"Daemon started at <commit>, cleared N gates, activated: [task labels]\"\n\nContext/KB properties:\n- Gate nodes are EXEMPT from semantic autowire entirely (structural, not semantic content)\n- Shared guidance: one note per gate_kind (registry lookup, not cosine), not 55 context edges\n- Fixes the hub-convergence problem: N independent dep paths instead of N tasks → 1 shared node\n\nWhy Option B (dispatcher creates): workers must not reason about graph shape. Wiring is enforced at dispatch time when the full DAG context is known.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T00:25:23.812Z","vec":[-0.09969986230134964,-0.02896474301815033,-0.04810592532157898,0.052605513483285904,0.03591297194361687,-0.04963907599449158,0.01470610685646534,-0.010037604719400406,-0.006493738852441311,0.08751282840967178,-0.01399074122